Q: runAsync() vs supplyAsync()

Ans: if we want to run background task asynchronously and do not want to return anything from that task,
then use CompletableFuture.runAsync() method. it takes runnable object
and return  CompletableFuture<Void>
    1:  CompletableFuture.runAsync(Runnable)
    2:  CompletableFuture.runAsync(Runnable, Executor)

if you want to run some background task asynchronously and want to return anything form task. we should use
 CompletableFuture.supplyAsync(). it takes a Supply<T> and return  CompletableFuture<T> where T is type of the value obtained by calling the given supplier.
 1:  CompletableFuture.supplyAsync(Supply<T>)
 2:  CompletableFuture.supplyAsync(Supplier<T>, Executor)
